-- title:
--   Collapse at level ℓ in characteristic ℓ
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field of prime characteristic $\ell$. Inside the field of Laurent series $K((q))$ one has the element `jqModC K`, namely the Hahn series $q^{-1}$ (the monomial `HahnSeries.single (-1 : ℤ) 1`) multiplied by the power series obtained from `jNum` by applying the ring map $\mathbb{Z} \to K$ to its coefficients, i.e. the $q$-expansion of the modular $j$-invariant read in $K$; for $N \neq 0$ one has `jqNModC K N`, the image of `jqModC K` under the operator `qExpand K N` (the level-$N$ change of variable on Laurent series), and the intermediate field `modularFunctionFieldC K N` of $K((q))$ over $K$ generated by the two-element set $\{$`jqModC K`, `jqNModC K N`$\}$. The theorem asserts the equality of intermediate fields $$\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\ K\ \ell = \mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\ K\ 1,$$ that is, adjoining $\bar j(q)$ and its level-$\ell$ transform to $K$ inside $K((q))$ gives the same subfield as adjoining $\bar j(q)$ and its level-$1$ transform. No hypothesis beyond $K$ being a field of characteristic $\ell$ with $\ell$ prime is imposed; in particular $K$ need not be perfect or algebraically closed.
--
--   This is the $q$-expansion shadow of Kronecker's congruence $\Phi_\ell(X,Y) \equiv (X^\ell - Y)(X - Y^\ell) \pmod{\ell}$: in characteristic $\ell$ the level-$\ell$ modular function field generated by $\bar j(q)$ and $\bar j(q^\ell)$ degenerates to the level-one field. It is used in the analysis of the characteristic-$\ell$ fibre of $X_0(\ell)$ at its nodes, for instance in the localisation and branch-normalisation statements for the node, and asserts nothing about schemes — only about subfields of $K((q))$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_modularFunctionFieldC_self_collapse_unconditional.lean

